window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0c53ef5188800731"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"improve-the-cloud-threat-model\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">改进云端威胁模型</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>如果生成的版本遗漏了安全假设或部署环境信息，请更新受监控代码库的威胁模型。本指南适用于 Codex Security Cloud。本地插件策略请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b?anchor=configure-the-scan\">配置扫描</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"what-a-threat-model-is\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">什么是威胁模型</h2> <p>威胁模型是对代码库工作方式的简短安全说明。Codex Security 会根据代码生成第一版草稿，并用它指导后续提交扫描和发现项的优先级排序。</p> <p>威胁模型会描述：</p> <ul> <li>入口点，以及谁可以向这些入口提供输入</li> <li>信任边界，以及身份验证或授权方面的假设</li> <li>敏感数据和特权操作</li> <li>需要特别关注的区域</li> </ul> <p>例如：</p> <blockquote> <p>面向公众的账户 API 接受已通过身份验证的用户提交的 JSON 请求和文件上传。用户只能更改自己所属租户中的账户。身份服务负责验证调用者身份，但每个处理程序都必须检查租户访问权限。计费更改由具有特权的内部服务处理。请优先检查租户权限校验是否缺失，以及是否存在可到达该服务的文件上传路径。</p> </blockquote> <p>请指出不确定的假设。例如，如果你希望评估的部署并非确实只允许内部访问，就不要把某个端点描述成“仅限内部”。</p> <p><a id=\"edit-the-threat-model\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">编辑威胁模型</h2> <ol> <li>打开 Codex Security Cloud 插件。如果尚未安装插件或配置提交监控，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">云端设置</a>。</li> <li>打开 <strong>Repositories（代码库）</strong>，选择受监控的代码库。</li> <li>打开 <strong>Monitoring settings（监控设置）</strong>。</li> <li>编辑 <strong>Threat model（威胁模型）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Save（保存）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>更改会应用于后续扫描。</p> <p>身份验证、租户边界或对外暴露的服务发生变化后，请重新检查威胁模型。将部署事实与扫描优先级分开记录。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"improve-the-cloud-threat-model\">Improve the Cloud threat model</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Update a monitored repository's threat model when the generated version misses security assumptions or deployment context. This guide applies to Codex Security Cloud. For local plugin policy, see <a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b?anchor=configure-the-scan\">Configure the scan</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"what-a-threat-model-is\">What a threat model is</h2> <p>A threat model is a short security summary of how your repository works. Codex Security creates the first draft from the code and uses it to guide future commit scans and prioritize findings.</p> <p>A threat model describes:</p> <ul> <li>Entry points and who can supply input to them</li> <li>Trust boundaries and authentication or authorization assumptions</li> <li>Sensitive data and privileged actions</li> <li>Areas that need particular attention</li> </ul> <p>For example:</p> <blockquote> <p>The public account API accepts authenticated users' JSON requests and file uploads. Users may change only accounts in their own tenant. The identity service authenticates the caller, but each handler must check tenant access. Billing changes go through a privileged internal service. Prioritize missing tenant checks and upload paths that can reach that service.</p> </blockquote> <p>Identify uncertain assumptions. For example, don't describe an endpoint as internal-only unless that is true of the deployment you want assessed.</p> <h2 id=\"edit-the-threat-model\">Edit the threat model</h2> <ol> <li>Open the Codex Security Cloud plugin. See <a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Cloud setup</a> if you haven't installed it or configured commit monitoring.</li> <li>Open <strong>Repositories</strong> and select the monitored repository.</li> <li>Open <strong>Monitoring settings</strong>.</li> <li>Edit <strong>Threat model</strong>, then select <strong>Save</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Changes apply to future scans.</p> <p>Revisit the model after changes to authentication, tenant boundaries, or exposed services. Keep facts about the deployment separate from priorities for the scan.</p>"};
